# E §5 example (synthetic), written out: "A benefit is paid monthly through 2027. A version known 2028-03-01 governs
# 2027 and cuts the benefit to 0": 500.00 PLN on day 15 of each month of 2027 (0 PLN from 2028, so nothing books).
# n: "The new version changes each 2027 instance by δ = -amount, recorded as twelve adjustments dated 2028-03-01":
# 12, and 12 * -500.00 = -6 000.00 PLN.
# f: "Had it written neither, every flows over the benefit's account from 2028-03-01 on would be a hole asking
# whether repayment is due" (HOLE-CHANGED, L §8.1 wording); konto's balance before 2028-03-01 stands: 6 000.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2028-06-30
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source act "benefit act"
source cut_act "the act that cuts it"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind benefits: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind waivers: event certain
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place payer: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input benefit: money PLN
input pay_dom: int

move pay[m in months]: benefits
  on day_of(m, pay_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from payer to konto amount benefit

version act_2027
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  benefit = 500.00 PLN governs 2027 "art. 1"
  benefit = 0 PLN governs 2028.. "art. 3: paid through 2027"
  pay_dom = 15 "art. 2"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2027-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version cut_2027
  cite cut_act
  governs 2027
  known 2028-03-01
  replace benefit = 0 PLN "art. 1"

ask n: count(a in adjustments over 2028-03-01), sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2028-03-01 where a.adjusts in benefits)
ask f: flows(konto, 2028-03)
ask g: bal(konto, 2028-02-29)
=== expect
f: ?"pay[2027-01] on 2027-01-15 changed after it was paid ...
...
  cut 2028-06-30
g: 6 000.00 PLN
...
  cut 2028-06-30
n: (12, -6 000.00 PLN)
  cut 2028-06-30
